  "system_answer": "是的，文档中确实存在对因员工留任问题导致机构知识流失的担忧。\n\n在'Bureau Cross-Cutting Management Objective 1.1 Risk Considerations'部分，文档明确指出：\n\n'Failure to modernize and strengthen DEIA in our global PM workforce and workplaces, provide our people with the necessary tools to succeed, or adapt to a post-pandemic posture will put at risk the Bureau's investments in recruiting, developing, and retaining the best talent in the long-term. The Bureau may lose people due to burnout, lack of work-life flexibilities, and frustrations over lack of DEIA representation, career mobility, and professional development opportunities.'\n\n此外，文档还提到：'Without much-needed IT and data modernization and infrastructure upgrades, the Bureau also risks losing talent due to an inflexible work environment and/or health concerns in a post-pandemic posture.'\n\n这些表述直接表明文档对员工留任（retention）问题存在担忧，担心因倦怠、缺乏工作生活弹性、职业发展机会不足等原因失去人才。\n\n同时，文档在'Bureau Cross-Cutting Management Goal 1'中强调要'improve knowledge management'（改进知识管理），这进一步暗示了机构对知识保留的重视，与人才流失风险相关联。\n\n因此，可以确认文档中存在对因员工留任问题导致机构知识流失的担忧。",
